    crm:P183i_has_representation <https://ids.lib.harvard.edu/ids/iiif/493338146/full/full/0/default.jpg> ;
    rdf:value """Monday, June 29, 1908
Fine. 
I lunched with Glaenzer and B.B. with Mme Lambert and Mrs. Rowland. He called on Mme de Luche and dined with St. André and Cardman. I called on Mrs. Baldwin, but did not see Gladys, who is ill with gastric fever. Dined alone. 
William James said, “When you climb on a man’s back, refrain from the temptation to spit on his head!” """^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 203 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1908> .

